  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Moutte is a fine sandy beach fringed with reeds, away from the centre. The La Moutte estate (Émile Ollivier's château) was donated to the Conservatoire du littoral in 1998 by his granddaughter Anne Troisier de Diaz; the town of Saint-Tropez has managed it since 2007. According to a third-party site (plages.tv), the beach stretches about 300 metres. The tourist office lists only the car park as an amenity and recommends bringing a picnic and fresh water.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Access is via the route des Salins then the chemin des Treilles de la Moutte (Gulf tourist office). According to an old third-party site (plages.tv, 2013), a barrier bars non-residents from driving in: you would need to park before it, then walk down (pedestrian passage allowed) — check on site.</p>
      <p>As on all the town's beaches, municipal order no. 1828/2026 of 6 July 2026 allows dogs on the town's beaches from 6am to 9.30am and 6.30pm to 10pm, from 16 July to 15 September 2026; outside those hours they are not allowed. Dogs must stay under their owner's constant responsibility and be kept on a leash when approaching other users and whenever circumstances require; the order does not apply to walkers with dogs on a leash on the coastal path. It only covers that period: for the rest of the year, we found no published rule, so rely on the signage on site. The tourist office listings for this beach, however, say "dogs are not allowed" with no mention of hours — probably listings not updated since the order, but that isn't guaranteed. Check the signage on site.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: bring fresh water and a picnic, as the tourist office recommends — no amenities are listed on site apart from the car park.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The La Moutte estate is the starting point of a walk along the coastal path (Conservatoire du littoral): see the <a href="/en/fiche-balade-sentier-littoral-moutte-salins-saint-tropez">coastal path</a> to <a href="/en/fiche-plage-salins-saint-tropez">Les Salins beach</a>. To the west lies <a href="/en/fiche-plage-canebiers-saint-tropez">Canebiers beach</a>.</p>
    </div>

